  "title": "She Wrote The Forfeit Rule. It Disqualified Her Own Kid.",
  "script": "A team mom on our rec soccer league decided only other teams should forfeit over scheduling conflicts. She cornered me, the volunteer scheduler, at pickup and demanded I add a clause to the league bylaws letting any coach formally challenge a forfeit within 48 hours for irregular scheduling influence. She copied the league president to ensure I complied. Fine. I added her clause exactly as dictated. Her son's team hit a bye-week conflict two rounds later. The opposing coach, copied on her original email, filed the exact challenge she had demanded. The league upheld it. Nobody raised a voice. Her son's team was disqualified from the tournament by the rule she wrote herself. At the banquet, she explained to twelve nine year olds why mom's rule beat them. The strictest referee was her own inbox.",
